# Android

Android is the public V1 platform (`DECISIONS.md` SPD-001).

## Recording and location

- The recording session state machine lives in shared C++. Android calls into it
  and renders its state. Do not duplicate session state in Java.
- A recording session continues in the background and with the screen off. It
  ends only when the user finishes it, the user discards it, or the OS
  terminates tracking unrecoverably (product spec §11.2).
- The location-permission rationale must connect the request to session
  recording. It must never be bundled with competition consent (spec §10 step
  3).
- Never claim continuous tracking outside an active session (spec §10 step 4).
- Adding `ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION` changes the Play Store data-safety
  declaration and requires justification. Add it only with measured evidence
  that it is required, and flag it for release governance.
- Background reliability across OEM skins is a measured fact, not an assumption.
  Do not write copy or code that assumes recording always survives.

## Telemetry and logging

- No PII, screenshots, or view hierarchies in telemetry. A screenshot of the map
  during a session is location data.
- No coordinates in logs reachable from a release build.
- Analytics are aggregate and contain no location values (spec §32, §34).

## Build configuration

- Product flavors are `google`, `web`, `fdroid`, `huawei`; build types are
  `debug`, `release`, `beta`. A change to build configuration must be considered
  for every combination.
- Build-time configuration reaches shared C++ through `BuildConfig` fields
  applied at platform initialisation. Follow the existing pattern rather than
  inventing a second one.
- No developer or private-network address may be the effective default in any
  build.
- Public builds must not present a purchase action, and must not expose
  Explorer Pro capabilities.

## Tests and style

- Follow `docs/JAVA_STYLE.md`.
- JVM unit tests live under `src/test/`. There is no instrumented test
  infrastructure; do not assume one exists, and do not add one as a side effect
  of another task.
- `./gradlew -Pandroidauto=true lint` is the lint gate.
